{
  "nodes": [
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_digitaloption_equity_digital_option","label":"Equity Digital Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_digitaloption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced analytically (Black-Scholes/Black76 cash-or-nothing formula) by default; alternatively priced as a call/put spread (difference of two vanilla equity options) when a more accurate reflection of the volatility smile is a priority than the closed-form analytic result."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_doublebarrieroption_equity_double_barrier_option","label":"Equity Double Barrier Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_doublebarrieroption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_doubletouchoption_equity_double_touch_option","label":"Equity Double Touch Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_doubletouchoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_europeanbarrieroption_equity_european_barrier_option","label":"Equity European Barrier Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_europeanbarrieroption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced by static replication rather than a closed-form barrier formula: a portfolio of a European option at strike K, a European option at the barrier B, and two digital options (payouts |B-K| and rebate R) reproduces the barrier payoff."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_europeancompositeoption_european_equity_composite_option","label":"European Equity Composite Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_europeancompositeoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced analytically under Black-Scholes by treating the payoff as depending on the product of correlated equity-spot and FX-spot GBM processes; the composite volatility is derived by combining equity and FX volatilities with their correlation, then applying the standard Black-Scholes-Merton formula with the payoff-currency risk-free rate."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_forward_equity_forward","label":"Equity Forward","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_forward.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_option_european_equity_option","label":"European Equity Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_option.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced with the Black76 analytic formula rather than raw Black-Scholes because the model is calibrated so the equity forward price follows drift-free GBM under the T-forward measure, matching today's fair forward price for maturity T."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_outperformanceoption_equity_outperformance_option","label":"Equity Outperformance Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_outperformanceoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_swap_equity_swap","label":"Equity Swap","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_swap.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced by discounting cashflows off the equity forwarding curve under an assumption of continuous, deterministic dividends; this is a known limitation since real dividends are discrete/on specific dates, making PV and P&L explain inaccurate and the model unsuitable for large trading books requiring precise desk/financial-control P&L attribution. The approach also ignores gap and wrong-way risk and capital-control/settlement events."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_touchoption_equity_touch_option","label":"Equity Touch Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_touchoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_varianceswap_equity_variance_swap","label":"Equity Variance and Volatility Swap","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_varianceswap.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced via a replicating-portfolio method: a variance swap can be statically replicated by a hedged portfolio of vanilla equity options across a range of strikes (put/call integral weighted by 1/K^2), so the numerical integration scheme/bounds (GaussLobatto vs Segment, Fixed vs PriceThreshold) directly determine pricing accuracy and speed. The companion volatility swap reuses the variance-swap replication and takes sqrt(E(Var)) as a proxy for E(sqrt(Var)), which by Jensen's inequality ignores convexity and systematically overestimates the volatility swap price; potential extensions would use local/stochastic vol models (e.g. Heston) with Monte Carlo or approximate analytics to correct this."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_equityoptionposition_equity_option_position","label":"Equity Option Position","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/equityoptionposition.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Price is derived directly from the prices of the underlying options (see European Equity Option pricing); basket weights are applied and, for multi-currency baskets, prices are converted to a common NPV currency (that of the first equity option in the basket) using current FX spot rates."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_equityposition_equity_position","label":"Equity Position","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/equityposition.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced directly from market quote(s) of the underlying share(s); basket weights are applied and multi-currency basket components are converted to a common NPV currency (that of the first equity in the basket) via current FX spot rates."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_europeanoptioncontingentonabarrier_european_option_contingent_on_a_barrier","label":"Vanilla European Option Contingent on a Barrier","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/europeanoptioncontingentonabarrier.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced using correlated Black-Scholes processes for the option underlying and the barrier underlying (each calibrated to its own ATM vol, linked via an externally supplied correlation), valued by Monte Carlo; if the option underlying is an IR asset class, Gaussian-Cam is used instead for the IR underlying since a simple GBM/Black-Scholes process cannot capture interest-rate term-structure dynamics. Product is classified MultiAssetOption when both underlyings are Equity/FX/COMM, or IrHybrid if the option underlying is IR."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_extendedaccumulator_extended_accumulator","label":"Extended Accumulator","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/extendedaccumulator.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Structured as a periodic forward-purchase (long party buys asset A at strike K on each fixing date) with a knock-out feature triggered by a barrier observed on a single Extension Decision Date, generalizing the accumulator payoff across FX, Equity, or Commodity underlyings."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_fx_accumulator_fx_accumulator","label":"FX Accumulator","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/fx_accumulator.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced with a Black-Scholes process calibrated to quoted market ATM volatility, valued via Monte Carlo simulation within the scripted trade framework."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_fx_americanoption_american_fx_option","label":"American FX Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/fx_americanoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Two pricing choices are offered: an approximate Barone-Adesi and Whaley model (fast, but assumes time-independent deal-strike volatility), or numerical Finite Difference Methods under Black-Scholes with time-dependent deal-strike volatility (more accurate, grid size/damping-step and time/spot discretization configurable); the current implementation assumes payoff at exercise."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_fx_asianoption_fx_asian_option","label":"FX Asian Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/fx_asianoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Implemented as a simplified wrapper around the more general Basket Option class in the scripted trade framework, priced via Monte Carlo simulation."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_fx_barrieroption_fx_barrier_option","label":"FX Barrier Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/fx_barrieroption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_fx_digitalbarrieroption_digital_fx_barrier_option","label":"Digital FX Barrier Option","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/fx_digitalbarrieroption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced using Finite Difference Methods under the Black-Scholes framework rather than a closed-form barrier formula, with parameters controlling grid size and damping steps to limit grid expansion."},
    {"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_models_black_model","label":"Black Model (Section models:black)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/models.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
